      "text": "We have 10 members in total, 5 boys and 5 girls. To find the probability that both chosen members are girls, we need to calculate the number of ways to choose 2 girls out of 5 and divide it by the number of ways to choose any 2 members out of 10.\n\nThe number of ways to choose 2 girls out of 5 can be calculated using the combination formula: \\(C(n, k) = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\\), where \\(n\\) is the total number of items, and \\(k\\) is the number of items to choose.\n\nSo, \\(C(5, 2) = \\frac{5!}{2!(5-2)!} = \\frac{5 \\times 4}{2 \\times 1} = 10\\).\n\nThe total number of ways to choose any 2 members out of 10 is \\(C(10, 2) = \\frac{10!}{2!(10-2)!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9}{2 \\times 1} = 45\\).\n\nTherefore, the probability that both chosen members are girls is \\(\\frac{10}{45} = \\frac{2}{9}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate combinations\ndef combinations(n, k):\n    return math.comb(n, k)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 2 girls out of 5\ngirls_combinations = combinations(5, 2)\n\n# Number of ways to choose any 2 members out of 10\ntotal_combinations = combinations(10, 2)\n\n# Probability that both chosen members are girls\nprobability = girls_combinations / total_combinations\nprint(probability)\n```\n```output\n0.2222222222222222\n```\nThe probability that both chosen members are girls is \\(\\frac{2}{9}\\), which is approximately 0.2222. \n\nSo, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{2}{9}}\\).",
