      "text": "To find the probability that two randomly chosen members of the club are both girls, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the total number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10.\n2. Determine the number of ways to choose 2 girls out of the 5 girls.\n3. Calculate the probability by dividing the number of favorable outcomes by the total number of outcomes.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10.**\n\nThe number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \\), where \\( n \\) is the total number of items, \\( k \\) is the number of items to choose, and \\( ! \\) denotes factorial.\n\nHere, \\( n = 10 \\) and \\( k = 2 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{2} = \\frac{10!}{2!(10-2)!} = \\frac{10!}{2!8!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 8!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9}{2 \\times 1} = 45\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 45 ways to choose 2 members out of 10.\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the number of ways to choose 2 girls out of 5.**\n\nUsing the combination formula again, where \\( n = 5 \\) and \\( k = 2 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{5}{2} = \\frac{5!}{2!(5-2)!} = \\frac{5!}{2!3!} = \\frac{5 \\times 4 \\times 3!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 3!} = \\frac{5 \\times 4}{2 \\times 1} = 10\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 10 ways to choose 2 girls out of 5.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the probability.**\n\nThe probability that both chosen members are girls is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of outcomes:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Number of ways to choose 2 girls}}{\\text{Total number of ways to choose 2 members}} = \\frac{10}{45} = \\frac{2}{9}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that the two chosen members are both girls is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{2}{9}}\\).",
